<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muridun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1144</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Muridun, 'disciples', were the followers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> teacher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-qasi">Ibn Qasi</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. In 1144 they rose against Almoravid rule, seizing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mertola">Mértola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silves">Silves</a> and other towns, and Ibn Qasi ruled Mértola as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>. Their revolt helped bring Almoravid power in al-Andalus to an end, but Ibn Qasi later allied with the Christian king of Portugal and was killed by his own followers in 1151.</p></div>
